<title>SINGAPORE: Bonvest 1996 net profit dips 4.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Bonvest 1996 net profit dips 4.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     22.59 vs  23.72</p>
<p>    Dividend (cts/shr)		    3.00 vs   3.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    10.69 vs  11.22</p>
<p>    Turnover				157.61 vs 153.65</p>
<p>    Other income incl interest	  3.02 vs   2.61</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		5.55 vs  4.72</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 31.02 vs  33.07</p>
<p>    Tax					8.46  vs  9.35</p>
<p>Note - Property-based Bonvest Holdings Ltd said rental income from flagship building Liat Towers would continue to contribute positively to results.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703305)</p>
</text>
